{"id": "EUVD-2026-82254", "enisaUuid": "0dd151a8-3b4a-372d-a0ab-940a4aa47e64", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntime/namespace: Validate nanosecond field in proc_timens_set_offset()\n\nThe function validates tv_sec to be within [-KTIME_SEC_MAX, KTIME_SEC_MAX]\nbut never validates that tv_nsec is within the valid range of\n[0, NSEC_PER_SEC-1] before using it in timespec64_add().\n\ntimespec64_add() expects both timespec64 structures to have normalized\nvalues with tv_nsec in the range [0, 999999999]. If off->val.tv_nsec\ncontains invalid values (negative or >= NSEC_PER_SEC), it could lead to\nincorrect calculations or unexpected behavior.\n\nAdd validation to ensure tv_nsec is within the valid range before\nperforming the addition.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b8a40de738b7c4896c2edbc6262bd1b3462ded0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b20d7085ab314672447322c10cc5d1ba443e3b8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db667d2970c756cc7b483f45f272440f845a665b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f0c3c0c36c7aedf55a60d9c71c4bd258b8937ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06aba58e58492d2b8eae059274caed29025ea96e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93146", "GHSA-477f-qmj2-58hm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "000f7986-59cc-3b77-8846-828a934fe787", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "061c4ca2-503b-331b-b987-93408f70b0a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04a8682a71becdb639ec9c0d82b315a2baef7a5d <db667d2970c756cc7b483f45f272440f845a665b"}, {"id": "1e44dc05-21d8-3945-8970-900cd5878e07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04a8682a71becdb639ec9c0d82b315a2baef7a5d <5b8a40de738b7c4896c2edbc6262bd1b3462ded0"}, {"id": "23ee0f46-73f9-30a0-9503-abfc8bfd8842", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "31f9909d-a28d-332a-8425-a171cdf47774", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4a2aea53-4d21-3598-973e-bea88426b214", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04a8682a71becdb639ec9c0d82b315a2baef7a5d <1f0c3c0c36c7aedf55a60d9c71c4bd258b8937ce"}, {"id": "66b20a66-888d-3dbd-8c76-e5922fb0c415", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04a8682a71becdb639ec9c0d82b315a2baef7a5d <b20d7085ab314672447322c10cc5d1ba443e3b8e"}, {"id": "73f556fe-d503-379e-b758-0f290bdd5e61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "9882078d-29a4-3fdb-8532-8df460737b34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04a8682a71becdb639ec9c0d82b315a2baef7a5d <06aba58e58492d2b8eae059274caed29025ea96e"}, {"id": "9c35c8ff-0cbe-354b-bbda-bd1bbdca7b7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "d2d271a7-0f93-35e2-a552-2c643a81ac6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "fd1da60e-73dd-39f1-a9b3-fede3b5d7dde", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "02a1dd41-bb04-3e1e-b523-65b4f20d08ef", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}